/-!
# Finite affine refinements of hypercovers of the small étale site

Let `X` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S` and let `B ⊆ Ob(X_étale)` be the set of étale
charts whose underlying scheme is affine. This file proves, for that `B`, the refinement
condition on coverings which the criterion of Stacks 0GMS case (2) asks of a set of objects:
every covering of a member of `B` can be refined by a *finite* covering whose members again lie
in `B`.

The content is that of Stacks 0218 — an étale covering of an affine scheme is refined by a
finite étale covering by affines — transported to the étale charts of an algebraic space and
repackaged. The geometry is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.exists_finite_affine_refinement`:
a covering sieve of an affine chart contains a finite covering family of affine charts. What is
added here is the packaging the criterion consumes, namely a pre-`0`-hypercover together with a
refinement morphism to the given one, with the index type in the universe `max u v` of the site.

Affineness of the object being covered is not a convenience: the objects of the small étale site
include infinite disjoint unions of affine charts, and a covering of such an object need have no
finite refinement at all.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.affineObjects`: the set of étale charts of `X` whose
  underlying scheme is affine.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.exists_finite_affine_hypercover_hom`: **a covering
  pre-`0`-hypercover of an affine étale chart admits a refinement by a finite covering
  pre-`0`-hypercover whose members are affine étale charts.** This is condition (2)(b) of
  Stacks 0GMS for the small étale site of an algebraic space, with `B` the affine charts.

## Implementation notes

The index type produced by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.exists_finite_affine_refinement`
is `Fin n`, while a `CategoryTheory.PreZeroHypercover` of the small étale site taken in the
sheaf universe of that site needs its index in `Type (u + 1)`; the two are reconciled by
`ULift`, which changes neither the generated sieve nor finiteness.

The refinement morphism is extracted from the containment of the generated sieve in the given
one: each structure morphism of the refinement lies in the sieve generated by the given
hypercover, hence factors through one of its members, and the factorisation is exactly the data
of a `CategoryTheory.PreZeroHypercover.Hom`.

### No `@[stacks 07U7]`

Stacks 07U7 asserts, for `X` quasi-compact and quasi-separated and `G` an `O_X`-module of finite
presentation, that `colim_i Hom_X(G, F_i) = Hom_X(G, colim_i F_i)`, and in particular that
`Hom_X(G, -)` commutes with filtered colimits in `QCoh(O_X)`. Neither assertion is proved here
and no attribute for it is carried. The result below is one of the three hypothesis checks that
the proof of Stacks 07U7 performs before invoking Stacks 0GN0, and a hypothesis check is not a
part of the statement being checked.

The displayed equality is a special case of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.InternalHom.`
`coyoneda_preservesColimitsOfShape_of_isFinitePresentation` (Stacks 0GN0), whose site hypothesis
is the one of Stacks 0GMR part (4), discharged for a set of objects by
`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.exists_set_isLocallySurjective_and_isQuasiCompact_prod_self`
(Stacks 0GMS case (2)) from conditions (2)(a), (2)(b), (2)(c). Three declarations are missing
for the chain to close:

* conditions (2)(a) and (2)(c) for the affine charts: that `∐_j h_{U_j}^# ⟶ *` is surjective for
  a finite family of affine charts, and that `h_U^# ⨯ h_{U'}^#` receives a surjection from a
  finite coproduct of sheafified representables of affine charts. Neither exists;
* a form of Stacks 0GN0 applicable to the small étale site. The library's form takes an
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.{u, u, u}`, whereas `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.`
  `smallEtaleRingedSite` is an `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.{u + 1, u, u}`: its objects lie one
  universe above its morphisms. The two cannot be unified, and the only universe transport in
  the tree, `Stacks.SheafOfModules.CoherentLift.liftRingedSite`, moves the sections universe and
  leaves the underlying category fixed.

The final assertion needs in addition that the inclusion `QCoh(O_X) ⥤ Mod(O_X)` commutes with
colimits, which is clause (2) of Stacks 0218's companion Stacks 03M1. No clause of Stacks 03M1 is
proved for an algebraic space: `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherent_colimit` is conditional
on the direct-sum and cokernel clauses of that same tag, both of which remain undischarged
hypotheses.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0218](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0218)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GMS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GMS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GMR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GMR)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-! ### Stacks 0218

`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_finite_affine_etale_refinement` is Stacks 0218: an étale covering of an
affine scheme is refined by a finite étale covering whose members are affine, each member of the
refinement being an affine open of a member of the original covering, which is the "moreover" of
the source. -/

add_to_stacks 0218 exists_finite_affine_etale_refinement

namespace Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u)

/-- The set of objects of the small étale site of `F` whose underlying scheme is affine.

This is the set `B ⊆ Ob(X_étale)` of affine objects which the proofs of Stacks 07U7 and of
Stacks 0GMS case (2) take as their covering set of objects. -/
def SmallEtale.affineObjects : Set (SmallEtale B S hS F) :=
  {W | IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W)}

/-- An object of the small étale site of `F` lies in `SmallEtale.affineObjects` if and only if its
underlying scheme is affine. -/
@[simp]
theorem SmallEtale.mem_affineObjects_iff {W : SmallEtale B S hS F} :
    W ∈ SmallEtale.affineObjects B S hS F ↔
      IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W) :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- **A covering of an affine étale chart is refined by a finite covering by affine étale
charts**, in pre-`0`-hypercover form.

If `U` is an étale chart of `F` with affine underlying scheme and `𝒰` is a pre-`0`-hypercover of
`U` whose sieve is covering for the small étale topology, then there is a pre-`0`-hypercover `𝒱`
of `U` refining `𝒰` whose sieve is covering, whose index type is finite, and all of whose
members have affine underlying scheme.

This is condition (2)(b) of Stacks 0GMS for the small étale site of an algebraic space with the
affine charts as the distinguished set of objects, and it is the content of Stacks 0218 on that
site. The underlying geometry is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.exists_finite_affine_refinement`; the refinement morphism
comes from the factorisation of each member of the finite family through a member of `𝒰`, which
the containment of sieves provides. -/
theorem SmallEtale.exists_finite_affine_hypercover_hom
    (U : SmallEtale B S hS F) (hU : U ∈ SmallEtale.affineObjects B S hS F)
    (𝒰 : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} U)
    (h𝒰 : 𝒰.sieve₀ ∈ SmallEtale.topology B S hS F U) :
    ∃ (𝒱 : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} U) (_ : 𝒱.Hom 𝒰),
      𝒱.sieve₀ ∈ SmallEtale.topology B S hS F U ∧ Finite 𝒱.I₀ ∧
        ∀ i, 𝒱.X i ∈ SmallEtale.affineObjects B S hS F := by
  obtain ⟨ι, hfin, V, f, hVaff, hle, hcov⟩ :=
    SmallEtale.exists_finite_affine_refinement B S hS F U hU 𝒰.sieve₀ h𝒰
  -- Each member of the finite affine family lies in the sieve of `𝒰`, hence factors through a
  -- member of `𝒰`; that factorisation is the refinement morphism.
  have key : ∀ k : ι, ∃ (j : 𝒰.I₀) (h : V k ⟶ 𝒰.X j), h ≫ 𝒰.f j = f k := by
    intro k
    obtain ⟨Y, g, p, hp, hfac⟩ := hle _ (Sieve.ofArrows_mk V f k)
    obtain ⟨j⟩ := hp
    exact ⟨j, g, hfac⟩
  choose jj hh hw using key
  -- Reindexing the family by `ULift` changes neither the presieve it generates nor finiteness.
  have hpre : Presieve.ofArrows (fun i : ULift.{u + 1} ι => V i.down) (fun i => f i.down) =
      Presieve.ofArrows V f := by
    refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
    · rintro Y g ⟨i⟩; exact ⟨i.down⟩
    · rintro Y g ⟨i⟩; exact ⟨ULift.up i⟩
  refine ⟨{ I₀ := ULift.{u + 1} ι, X := fun i => V i.down, f := fun i => f i.down },
    { s₀ := fun i => jj i.down, h₀ := fun i => hh i.down, w₀ := fun i => hw i.down },
    ?_, inferInstance, fun i => hVaff i.down⟩
  show Sieve.generate (Presieve.ofArrows _ _) ∈ _
  rw [hpre]
  exact hcov

end Space

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
